{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "error (ambiguous): what does \"the square root of\" apply to\nambiguous: set args.assume.scope to one of:\n  1) sqrt(x) + ... (default)\n  2) sqrt(x + ...)\nrepeat the request with args.assume.scope set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default; or: say \"the square root of the quantity ...\" for the second"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": false, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "what is the square root of x plus 1?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": [], "understood": false}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "", "error": {"code": "ambiguous", "message": "what does \"the square root of\" apply to", "key": "scope", "readings": [{"index": 1, "reading": "sqrt(x) + ...", "default": true}, {"index": 2, "reading": "sqrt(x + ...)", "default": false}], "how": "repeat the request with args.assume.scope set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default; or: say \"the square root of the quantity ...\" for the second"}}, "isError": true}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x) = sqrt(x + 1)\n  ucas: show it\nit(x: real) = sqrt(x + 1)\n  -> real\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "what is the square root of x plus 1?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = sqrt(x + 1)", "show it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "show", "definition": "it(x: real) = sqrt(x + 1)", "body": "sqrt(x + 1)", "type": "real"}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "what does \"the square root of\" apply to: sqrt(x + ...) (args.assume.scope)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x) = sqrt(x + 1)\n  ucas: show it\nit(x: real) = sqrt(x + 1)\n  -> real\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "error (ambiguous): \"odd\"\nambiguous: set args.assume.question to one of:\n  1) an odd function, f(-x) = -f(x) (default)\n  2) an odd number for every input\nrepeat the request with args.assume.question set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default; or: say \"an odd function\" or \"always odd\""}], "structuredContent": {"id": 5, "ok": false, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "is x odd for u8 x?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": [], "understood": false}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "", "error": {"code": "ambiguous", "message": "\"odd\"", "key": "question", "readings": [{"index": 1, "reading": "an odd function, f(-x) = -f(x)", "default": true}, {"index": 2, "reading": "an odd number for every input", "default": false}], "how": "repeat the request with args.assume.question set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default; or: say \"an odd function\" or \"always odd\""}}, "isError": true}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 6, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: odd for every input when the range is 1..1\n  ucas: it(x: u8) = x\n  ucas: lhs(x: u8) = it(x) % 2\n  ucas: range lhs\nrange of lhs -> u8:\n  0..1   (2 distinct values)\n  values: 0..1\n  fits in u1\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "\u001eanswer 2\nis x odd for u8 x?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x: u8) = x", "lhs(x: u8) = it(x) % 2", "range lhs"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "range", "type": "u8", "empty": false, "exhaustive": true, "points": 256, "undefined_points": 0, "min": {"value": 0, "exact": "0"}, "max": {"value": 1, "exact": "1"}, "distinct": 2, "values": [0, 1], "fits": "u1"}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "info", "text": "odd for every input when the range is 1..1"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "every point of the domain evaluated"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: odd for every input when the range is 1..1\n  ucas: it(x: u8) = x\n  ucas: lhs(x: u8) = it(x) % 2\n  ucas: range lhs\nrange of lhs -> u8:\n  0..1   (2 distinct values)\n  values: 0..1\n  fits in u1\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "monotonic x^3 - 3x:\n  not monotonic on all real x\n  maximal intervals of monotonicity:\n    x in (-inf, -1]: increasing\n    x in [-1, 1]: decreasing\n    x in [1, inf): increasing\n  witness: x = -2 < x = -1 but f(-2) = -2 < f(-1) = 2 (not decreasing)\n  witness: x = -1 < x = 1 but f(-1) = 2 > f(1) = -2 (not increasing)\n  proved symbolically: x^3 - 3x' = 3x^2 - 3; its real roots: -1, 1 (exact); f' keeps its sign between roots of odd multiplicity\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "monotonic", "ucas": "monotonic x^3 - 3x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "monotonic", "var": "x", "verdict": "not monotonic", "on": "all real x", "intervals": [{"lo": null, "hi": -1, "direction": "increasing", "strict": true}, {"lo": -1, "hi": 1, "direction": "decreasing", "strict": true}, {"lo": 1, "hi": null, "direction": "increasing", "strict": true}], "witness_not_decreasing": [-2, -1], "witness_not_increasing": [-1, 1]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "symbolic", "text": "proved symbolically: x^3 - 3x' = 3x^2 - 3; its real roots: -1, 1 (exact); f' keeps its sign between roots of odd multiplicity"}, "files": [], "text": "monotonic x^3 - 3x:\n  not monotonic on all real x\n  maximal intervals of monotonicity:\n    x in (-inf, -1]: increasing\n    x in [-1, 1]: decreasing\n    x in [1, inf): increasing\n  witness: x = -2 < x = -1 but f(-2) = -2 < f(-1) = 2 (not decreasing)\n  witness: x = -1 < x = 1 but f(-1) = 2 > f(1) = -2 (not increasing)\n  proved symbolically: x^3 - 3x' = 3x^2 - 3; its real roots: -1, 1 (exact); f' keeps its sign between roots of odd multiplicity\n"}, "isError": false}}
